{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Schwartz&limit=10&title=Shielded","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"titleInfo":[{"title":"Shielded","subTitle":"how the police became untouchable"},{"@type":"alternative","title":"How the police became untouchable"}],"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Schwartz, Joanna C.","role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author."}}]},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2023"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2023"},"issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"[New York, New York] :"}},"publisher":"Viking,","dateIssued":[2023]}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"xxi, 308 pages ; 24 cm"},"abstract":[{"@type":"Summary","#text":"\"An urgent and definitive examination of how the legal system prevents accountability for police misconduct, from one of the country's leading scholars on policing\"--"},{"@type":"Summary","#text":"Despite recent high-profile murders that have brought attention to the pervasiveness of police misconduct, it remains nearly impossible to hold police accountable for abuses of power. Schwartz exposes the myriad ways in which our legal system protects police at all costs, with analysis about subjects ranging from qualified immunity to no-knock warrants. She paints a compelling picture of the human cost of our failing criminal justice system, and reveals what tragically familiar calls for \"justice\" truly entail. -- adapted from jacket"}],"tableOfContents":"How we got here -- Lawyers -- The complaint -- The Constitution -- Qualified immunity -- Suing the city -- Judges -- Juries -- Court-ordered reforms -- Officers' bank accounts -- Local government budgets -- Learning from lawsuits -- A better way.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Joanna Schwartz."},"Place of publication from publisher's website.",{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Tort liability of police","geographic":"United States"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Police misconduct","Law and legislation"],"geographic":"United States"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Privileges and immunities","geographic":"United States"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"POLITICAL SCIENCE / Law Enforcement"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"LAW / Civil Rights"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"POLITICAL SCIENCE / Corruption & Misconduct"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":["Police misconduct","Law and legislation"]},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Privileges and immunities"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Tort liability of police"},{"@authority":"sears","topic":"Police corruption"},{"@authority":"fast","geographic":"United States"},{"topic":"Qualified immunity."}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"KF1307 .S39 2023"},{"@edition":"23/eng/20230105","@authority":"ddc","#text":"344.7305/2"}],"relatedItem":[{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Online version:","@displayLabel":"Online version:","titleInfo":{"title":"Shielded"},"name":{"namePart":"Schwartz, Joanna C."},"originInfo":{"publisher":"[New York, New York] : Viking, [2023]"},"identifier":[{"@type":"local","#text":"(DLC)  2022053634"},{"@